<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="nl">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="light">
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#800000">
    {{! The homepage needs a title of its own: the client's, not the site name.
        The article list needs one too - and there is no context to key on: a
        collection written in routes.yaml renders with an *empty* context (the
        debug in this theme printed "home,index" for the front page, "tag" for a
        tag archive, and nothing at all for /artikelen/), so no is-check can see
        it and meta_title is the site name there. `url` is set on every route, so
        the list is named by its URL instead. (No mustaches in this comment:
        Handlebars ends a comment at the first closing brace pair, and anything
        after it becomes template again.) }}
    <title>{{#is "home"}}{{@custom.home_meta_title}}{{else}}{{#match (url) "=" "/artikelen/"}}Artikelen - {{@site.title}}{{else}}{{meta_title}}{{/match}}{{/is}}</title>

    {{!-- Ghost writes the canonical, the description, the Open Graph and
          Twitter tags and the structured data here.

          "exclude" keeps Ghost's two frontend apps off the site: Portal (the
          membership signup widget, 665 KiB from jsDelivr) and Sodo Search (86
          KiB). This client has no memberships and no search box, so both were
          pure weight - together they were most of a mobile page load, and
          Portal's data fetching against a memberless site also logged three
          403s and an exception in the console. --}}
    {{ghost_head exclude="portal,search"}}

    {{> "structured-data"}}

    <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{asset "built/screen.css"}}">
    <link rel="preload" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin href="{{asset "fonts/rubik-latin.woff2"}}">
</head>
<body class="{{body_class}} font-sans">

    {{!-- The first tab stop on the page: the header carries six links and a
          button, and this is the way past them. --}}
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Naar de inhoud</a>

    {{> "header"}}

    <main id="main" tabindex="-1">
        {{{body}}}
    </main>

    {{> "footer"}}

    <script src="{{asset "js/main.js"}}" defer></script>
    {{ghost_foot}}
</body>
</html>
